WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.955 --> 00:00:15.715
For many days Oliver remained indoors with Fagin.

2
00:00:16.656 --> 00:00:20.937
The other boys brought home a great number of handkerchiefs, so he was kept busy picking out the

3
00:00:20.977 --> 00:00:25.358
monograms. Every morning Charley and the Dodger played their game with Fagin.

4
00:00:26.398 --> 00:00:31.100
Sometimes Oliver joined in, trying to take an item from Fagin before he felt a hand in his

5
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.457
pocket. Oliver began to long for fresh air.

6
00:00:35.337 --> 00:00:38.178
He begged Fagin to allow him to go out to work with the others.

7
00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.860
But Fagin said he wasn't ready yet.

8
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:47.062
Whenever the boys came home empty-handed, Fagin lectured them on the misery of idleness and lazy habits.

9
00:00:48.183 --> 00:00:52.284
Then he reinforced the importance of hard work by sending them to bed without supper.

10
00:00:53.425 --> 00:00:57.166
Seeing this, Oliver was even more anxious to be actively employed.

11
00:00:58.227 --> 00:01:00.648
For several days there were no handkerchiefs to work on.

12
00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:04.965
Then suddenly one morning, Fagin gave Oliver permission to go out.

13
00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:10.968
"I think today would be a good day for you to begin working, my dear," said Fagin.

14
00:01:10.988 --> 00:01:13.949
"Will I be making wallets or handkerchiefs?"

15
00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:15.550
Oliver asked innocently.

16
00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.572
Charley had another coughing fit over his coffee while the Dodger merely smiled.

17
00:01:20.592 --> 00:01:26.074
"Just follow Charley and the Dodger, and do whatever the Dodger tells you," said Fagin.

18
00:01:26.974 --> 00:01:29.215
"Remember, use him as your model."

19
00:01:30.235 --> 00:01:31.276
And so they went out.

20
00:01:32.412 --> 00:01:34.373
Oliver walked between the Dodger and Charley.

21
00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:40.296
They walked so slowly that Oliver soon began to think his companions were planning to deceive Fagin by

22
00:01:40.376 --> 00:01:41.637
not going to work at all.

23
00:01:42.637 --> 00:01:46.839
As they walked along, the Dodger pulled caps from the heads of small boys and tossed them out

24
00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:47.299
of reach.

25
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.302
Charley took apples and onions from the market stalls and stuffed them into his surprisingly large pockets.

26
00:01:54.343 --> 00:01:56.224
This behavior looked very bad to Oliver.

27
00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:02.004
He was about to announce that he'd find his own way back to Fagin's when suddenly the Dodger

28
00:02:02.044 --> 00:02:05.667
stopped. He put his finger on his lip to silence the others.

29
00:02:06.748 --> 00:02:07.469
"What's the matter?"

30
00:02:07.809 --> 00:02:08.550
demanded Oliver.

31
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.932
"Hush!" said the Dodger.

32
00:02:10.952 --> 00:02:13.934
"Do you see that old man outside the bookseller's?"

33
00:02:14.995 --> 00:02:16.156
"The old gentleman over there?"

34
00:02:16.537 --> 00:02:17.137
said Oliver.

35
00:02:17.157 --> 00:02:19.239
"Yes, I see him."

36
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.641
"He'll do," said the Dodger.

37
00:02:21.661 --> 00:02:25.884
"A prime one," observed Charley.

38
00:02:25.944 --> 00:02:30.286
Oliver looked from one to the other with surprise, but he didn't dare ask any questions.

39
00:02:31.426 --> 00:02:35.908
Charley and the Dodger walked stealthily across the road and slunk close behind the old gentleman.

40
00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:42.091
Oliver walked a few paces after them and, not knowing what to do, looked on in silent amazement.

41
00:02:43.051 --> 00:02:48.394
The old gentleman was a very respectable-looking person with gold spectacles and an elegant bamboo cane.

42
00:02:50.074 --> 00:02:54.620
He had picked up a book from a table outside the bookseller's and there he stood, reading away

43
00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.881
as if he were sitting at home.

44
00:02:56.981 --> 00:02:59.202
He didn't appear to notice the street or the boys.

45
00:03:00.162 --> 00:03:04.543
Instead he stared only at the book, which he seemed to be reading with the greatest interest and

46
00:03:04.663 --> 00:03:11.345
eagerness. Suddenly, to Oliver's horror, the Dodger plunged his hand into the old man's pocket and pulled out

47
00:03:11.385 --> 00:03:12.025
a handkerchief.

48
00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:17.127
The Dodger handed it to Charley, and the two of them ran around the corner at full speed.

49
00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:23.901
In that instant Oliver understood the whole mystery of the handkerchiefs, the watches, the jewelry, and the "work"

50
00:03:23.921 --> 00:03:25.302
that the boys did for Fagin.

51
00:03:26.282 --> 00:03:29.404
He stood for a moment with the blood tingling through his veins from terror.

52
00:03:30.385 --> 00:03:31.885
He felt as if he were on fire.

53
00:03:32.846 --> 00:03:36.228
Then, confused and frightened, he ran away as fast as he could.

54
00:03:37.929 --> 00:03:39.450
This all happened in an instant.

55
00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:45.013
At the very moment when Oliver began to run, the old gentleman put his hand into his pocket.

56
00:03:46.013 --> 00:03:48.514
He discovered his handkerchief was missing and turned around.

57
00:03:49.675 --> 00:03:53.694
Seeing Oliver running away, he naturally concluded that Oliver was the thief.

58
00:03:54.814 --> 00:03:55.695
"Stop, thief!"

59
00:03:56.115 --> 00:03:59.778
shouted the old gentleman as he took off after Oliver with the book still in his hand.

60
00:04:00.739 --> 00:04:03.280
The old gentleman was not the only one who cried out.

61
00:04:04.361 --> 00:04:08.564
Charley and the Dodger had not wanted to attract attention by running down the open street.

62
00:04:09.645 --> 00:04:12.166
They had merely hidden in the first doorway around the corner.

63
00:04:13.247 --> 00:04:17.930
As soon as they saw Oliver running and heard the old gentleman shouting, they knew what had happened.

64
00:04:19.111 --> 00:04:19.912
"Stop, thief!"

65
00:04:20.256 --> 00:04:22.038
they shouted as they joined in the pursuit.

66
00:04:23.138 --> 00:04:24.680
This upset Oliver even more.

67
00:04:25.621 --> 00:04:30.244
So away he went like the wind with the old gentleman and the two boys roaring and shouting

68
00:04:30.284 --> 00:04:30.785
behind him.

69
00:04:32.506 --> 00:04:34.988
Hearing the commotion, the baker threw down his basket.

70
00:04:35.789 --> 00:04:37.110
The milkman left his pail.

71
00:04:37.971 --> 00:04:39.832
The errand boy abandoned his parcels.

72
00:04:40.893 --> 00:04:42.234
The tradesman left his counter.

73
00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:46.157
Away they all ran after Oliver, with everyone shouting.

74
00:04:47.238 --> 00:04:47.999
"Stop, thief!

75
00:04:48.499 --> 00:04:49.340
Stop, thief!"

76
00:04:50.348 --> 00:04:53.209
The cry was taken up by what seemed like a hundred voices.

77
00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:57.351
At last a man caught up to Oliver and dragged him to the ground.

78
00:04:57.371 --> 00:04:59.492
"Give the boy some air!"

79
00:04:59.853 --> 00:05:00.513
cried the baker.

80
00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.254
"Nonsense! He doesn't deserve it!"

81
00:05:03.594 --> 00:05:04.255
said the milkman.

82
00:05:04.275 --> 00:05:06.536
"Here comes the old man!"

83
00:05:06.956 --> 00:05:07.796
said the errand boy.

84
00:05:07.816 --> 00:05:09.797
"Is this the boy, sir?"

85
00:05:10.137 --> 00:05:10.878
asked the tradesman.

86
00:05:11.858 --> 00:05:15.180
Covered with mud and bleeding from his lip, Oliver lay on the ground.

87
00:05:16.852 --> 00:05:21.134
He looked wildly at the faces surrounding him while the old gentleman was dragged into the circle.

88
00:05:22.195 --> 00:05:24.856
"Yes," said the old gentleman, looking Oliver in the eye.

89
00:05:24.876 --> 00:05:27.017
"I am afraid it is the boy."

90
00:05:27.037 --> 00:05:29.659
"Afraid!" murmured the crowd.

91
00:05:30.619 --> 00:05:31.440
"That's a good one!"

92
00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:35.522
"Poor fellow, he has hurt himself," said the old gentleman.

93
00:05:35.542 --> 00:05:40.365
"I did that, sir, and I cut my knuckle against his teeth," said a burly fellow.

94
00:05:40.385 --> 00:05:42.226
"I stopped him, sir."

95
00:05:43.186 --> 00:05:46.548
He touched his hat with a grin, expecting some reward for his pains.

96
00:05:47.552 --> 00:05:50.354
But the old gentleman eyed him with an expression of dislike.

97
00:05:51.395 --> 00:05:53.977
The old gentleman looked as if he wanted to run away too.

98
00:05:55.058 --> 00:05:59.182
But at that moment a police officer made his way through the crowd and seized Oliver by the

99
00:05:59.222 --> 00:06:02.825
collar. "Come on, get up," the policeman said roughly.

100
00:06:02.845 --> 00:06:05.567
"It wasn't me, sir.

101
00:06:06.468 --> 00:06:09.590
Indeed it was two other boys," said Oliver, looking around.

102
00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.492
"They're here somewhere."

103
00:06:11.512 --> 00:06:14.394
"Oh, no, they aren't," said the policeman.

104
00:06:15.435 --> 00:06:20.114
And he was right, because Charley and the Dodger had disappeared down the first alley they'd come to.

105
00:06:20.134 --> 00:06:22.895
"Get up," said the policeman again.

106
00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:26.397
"Don't hurt him," said the old gentleman with concern.

107
00:06:26.417 --> 00:06:30.740
"Oh, I wouldn't think of hurting him," said the policeman sarcastically.

108
00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.521
"Will you stand upon your legs, you young devil?"

109
00:06:34.522 --> 00:06:37.803
Oliver did not reply, but instead tried to rise to his feet.

110
00:06:38.784 --> 00:06:42.886
The policeman grabbed Oliver's jacket collar and dragged him down the street at a rapid pace.

111
00:06:43.947 --> 00:06:48.476
The old gentleman walked by the policeman's side, and the crowd followed along behind.
